course: dictionary
lesson: 9463
title: Starry: full of stars, and more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Starry comes from star, so it often describes something full of stars. «The children lay on the grass and counted the stars in the starry sky.» Here starry means full of stars, or lit by stars.
explain: Starry can also mean shining like stars. «The starry lights on the Christmas tree sparkled in the dark.» The lights are not stars, but they glitter the same way. Look at the clues around the word to choose the right meaning.
explain: Starry-eyed is a special phrase. «Maya was starry-eyed about her trip, sure it would be perfect and not noticing the problems.» Starry-eyed means hopeful and dreamy. Context often shows you which meaning an author wants.
fact: Starry is an adjective: starry, starrier, starriest.
fact: «Starry» means full of stars, or lit by stars, as in «a starry night».
fact: «Starry» can also mean shining like stars, or sparkling.
fact: «Starry-eyed» means hopeful and dreamy, not seeing problems.
fact: «The Starry Night» is a famous painting by Vincent van Gogh, painted in 1889; «a starry cast» (informal) means a group of famous people.
exercise: «The dung beetles went straight even under a starry sky in a planetarium.» What does starry mean here? | *Full of stars, or lit by stars | Covered in mud and dung | Very loud and noisy | Hungry for food
exercise: Maya was «starry-eyed» about her trip. What does starry-eyed mean? | Eyes that were full of tears | Tired after a long night | *Hopeful and dreamy, not seeing problems | Angry with everyone around her
exercise: «The film had a starry cast of famous actors.» What does starry mean in this sentence? | Dirty and messy | Very dark and cold | Full of stars in the sky | *To do with famous people, an informal meaning
test: «The glowworms made the cave ceiling look like a starry sky.» What does the sentence suggest? | The ceiling was covered in mud | The cave was flooded with water | *The ceiling looked full of tiny lights | The ceiling was painted plain white
test: Which phrase means hopeful and dreamy? | starry sky | starry cast | starry night | *starry-eyed
exam: Which meaning of starry fits «a starry cast of actors» best? | *Famous people, an informal meaning | Hopeful and dreamy | Shining like a diamond | Full of stars in the sky
